what's going on guys this is rob and  welcome back to the rumor roundup our  weekly series where we cover all the  news and rumors that you may have missed  over the course of the week  and under normal circumstances we cover  video games  tv shows all kinds of cool things but if  we're being honest with ourselves  this week there's only one news story  worth talking about  and it's that scarlett johansson has  filed a lawsuit  against disney now why did this happen  well according to the lawsuit as it was  filed in los angeles  a good portion of scarlett johansson's  salary was tied to the box office  performance  of the black widow film it's estimated  and i'm not going to swear by this  number but it's estimated that scarlett  johansson has lost 50 million dollars as  a result of the movie  being released on streaming services and  theaters at the same time  now we'll get into what kevin feige and  all these guys have to say about this  here in a second  but here's the reason why this is such a  big deal before covet 19 there was just  kind of an alliance between hollywood  production studios  and movie theaters that hollywood  studios were making films but of what  use is a film if there's nobody there to  see it  enter movie theaters that provided a  means by which these films could be seen  that were being made by hollywood  studios the kind of agreement that was  essentially struck here over the years  is that the ticket proceeds from these  movie sales would go to the hollywood  film studios  and the theaters themselves would make  money on concessions now all this  changed with covid19 although if we're  being honest with ourselves  this all really started with netflix but  all this changed with covid19 when we  all experienced the covid quarantine  lockdown  of 2020. we couldn't go anywhere and you  had all these hollywood film studios  that had spent hundreds of millions of  dollars on these movies that were  literally just sitting in a vault or on  somebody's desk in an editing room table  and the reality is while releasing it on  a streaming service  would not garner anywhere near as much  money as that would make in a theatrical  release  fifty percent of something is better  than a hundred percent of nothing and we  couldn't go to movie theaters anyway so  they started releasing them on streaming  services  now at the time nobody had any qualms  about this it just made good business  sense  but once the quarantine lockdowns ended  the expectation  is that we would go back to business as  usual we would have movies that were  made by hollywood studios that would be  released in theaters  they would enjoy a theatrical run of  usually between four to six months  depending on the film  and then would be released to some kind  of a streaming service whether it was  owned by that hollywood production  studio  or some other studio that it was  licensed to what disney did here is by  releasing a movie on a streaming service  and a theater at the same time  it basically blackballed movie theaters  and that's why you see the movie theater  associations and all these major  companies coming out and saying  no this can't be allowed to happen  because it will quite literally  kill the industry now there's a lot of  unanswered questions here specifically  when it comes to why people chose to  watch black widow on a streaming service  instead of in the theaters  honestly there's a lot of people who are  traveling now a lot of people are still  afraid to go out due to the delta  variant that's basically going around  right now so  we don't necessarily have a definitive  answer as to why people enjoyed  the streaming service version of black  widow as opposed to the theatrical run  but what we do know is that when black  widow first opened up in theaters it had  a huge weekend  and then it immediately dropped off and  as a lot of you guys know from your own  casual reading  black widow had the single worst  drop-off of  any movie that's ever been released to  theaters from the marvel cinematic  universe  and so this whole idea of disney  throwing black widow on a streaming  service  from the movie theater's perspective  represents a clear and present danger to  the survival  of movie theaters themselves now the  other big thing about this  is that this will determine how it is  that we have actors actresses  and even staff members in hollywood  going forward in terms of how they  signed contracts  with hollywood production studios in  much the same way that in years past  a lot of people signed contracts with  hollywood film studios  based on the net proceeds of the film  and then the books were cooked to make  it look like the movie didn't actually  make any money so they were basically  left hanging with a zero dollar paycheck  robin williams and aladdin the thing  that a lot of people are doing now is  they're coming forward and they're  saying  no like i want to sign a contract based  on the gross theatrical proceeds of the  film  so that they're basically guaranteed to  walk home with a paycheck scarlett  johansson  did that but the lawsuit seems to allege  that the contract was signed between  scarlett johansson  and marvel but disney is the parent  company more so than that  the lawsuit indicates that disney  actually forced marvel to release the  movie  on disney plus now the reason why this  is such a big talking point is because a  lot of actors actresses  and even members of the marvel cinematic  universe are coming out and saying  something specifically  kevin feige who seems to basically side  with scarlett johansson  now this bit of information comes from  hollywood reporter editor matthew  baloney who basically covered the  concerns of kevin feige in a newsletter  that was previously written  and i quote here feige is not a company  man and not prone to corporate showdowns  or shouting matches but i'm told  he's angry and embarrassed he lobbied  disney against the day-and-date plan for  black widow  preferring the big screen exclusivity  and not wanting to upset his talent  and then when the [ __ ] hit the fan the  movie started tanking and johansen's  team threatened litigation  he wanted disney to make this right with  her now the indication here is that  kevin feige again  sides with scarlett johansson that he  seems to look out for his actresses and  his actors and his staff  more so than that kevin feige went on  record in previously saying that having  a movie from the marvel cinematic  universe released in theaters  offers a kind of experience that you  simply just can't get at home  and that's an accurate statement how  different would infinity war and  avengers in-game have been  if you were sitting at home watching it  on your tv versus sitting in the movie  theater  and it's not just the sound system it's  not just the gigantic screen  it's the audience it's the people who  are there you guys remember the  reactions of everybody and in fact i  still go back and watch them now  the scene where captain america lifted  thor's hammer when t'challa returned  these are all moments that you would not  be able to experience in the same way  had you not seen it in theaters  [Applause]  so there is a benefit to seeing not just  mcu movies  but movies as a whole in theaters that  you simply just can't experience  by seeing it at home now in response to  this whole lawsuit  disney did fire back although the  response has more or less been  criticized  by basically everybody so the statement  released by disney in part  reads like this there is no merit  whatsoever to this filing the lawsuit is  especially sad and distressing in its  callous disregard  for the horrific and prolonged global  effects of the covet 19 pandemic  disney has fully complied with ms  johansen's contract  and furthermore the release of black  widow on disney plus with premier access  has significantly enhanced her ability  to earn additional compensation  on top of the 20 million dollars she's  received to date now we don't know  exactly what this means there was some  kind of a secondary contract that was  signed between scarlett johansson and  disney so that she would receive a  portion of the proceeds of black widow  regardless of what platform it was  released on whether it was in theaters  or on disney plus but if that's the case  why would she file a lawsuit in the  first place  the important thing to take away from  all this though is that this lawsuit  regardless of how it turns out  is going to have a massive impact on the  film industry as a whole  there's no real going back from this and  it could potentially set a massive  precedent  that when a movie is released on a  streaming service and it's released in  theaters that now actors and actresses  have bargaining power they have  precedent here that they can go forward  and they can say look we get the  streaming services are the future  we get that there's going to be a time  whereby movies  are released in theaters and in  streaming services if movie theaters  can't find a way to cope with that  that's their problem that's not the  problem of the hollywood film studios  and so if that's the case they now have  the ability to collectively bargain or  to operate individually and to say  we want to make our money based on the  gross proceeds of not just the  theatrical run  but the streaming service as well and so  how this turns out is going to be  anybody's guess and i'm interested i'm  very very very curious here  but regardless that's our episode for  this week again only one real topic  worth talking about  scarlett johansson suing disney but  thank you guys for watching if there's  any news we missed make sure you guys  let us know down in the comment section  and we will catch you all later peace

